WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.330
Have you ever had a smartphone freeze up on you?

2
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:10.550
Imagine trying to fix that glitching screen by taking a heavy steel hammer and smashing

3
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:11.230
the device.

4
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:12.490
It sounds ridiculous.

5
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.910
Yet for the last hundred years, this is essentially how we have treated the human body.

6
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:24.670
We use lab-made synthetic chemicals as blunt physical tools, forcing specific cellular

7
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.630
switches to flip on or off.

8
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.510
But our bodies are highly connected networks.

9
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.750
When a foreign chemical forces one single switch, the rest of the network resists.

10
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.850
It rings alarm bells across the system, creating the secondary problems we commonly call

11
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:40.410
side effects.

12
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.550
We treat ourselves like simple mechanical engines, to be bullied into working.

13
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.610
By ignoring the system as a whole, our treatments frequently damage the very things they

14
00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:51.450
are trying to repair.

15
00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:56.610
To move forward, we need to stop hitting the hardware with a hammer and start writing

16
00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:57.730
a software update.

17
00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:01.130
This approach is called Instructional Medicine.

18
00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:03.450
Instead of inventing alien chemicals,

19
00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.890
we use the precise three-dimensional proteins the body naturally produces.

20
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.630
Think of these proteins as lines of code that tell your cells exactly how to heal.

21
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:18.130
When we provide the exact signals the system evolved to recognize, we are finally speaking

22
00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.330
the body's native language, rather than shouting over it.

23
00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:27.070
If the human body already makes these perfect healing instructions, you might wonder why

24
00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.090
we don't just put them in a pill.

25
00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:31.510
The answer comes down to physics.

26
00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.450
These signaling proteins are incredibly delicate.

27
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.590
Their ability to deliver a message relies entirely on their exact, folded three-dimensional

28
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:42.170
shape.

29
00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.290
If that shape unravels, the instruction is gone.

30
00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:48.570
Think about an egg white hitting a hot frying pan.

31
00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.770
The clear liquid turns white and solid because the heat permanently scrambles the proteins

32
00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:54.370
inside.

33
00:01:54.940 --> 00:02:00.490
Traditional drug manufacturing relies on the same intense heat and harsh solvents to sterilize

34
00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:01.050
medicines.

35
00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.650
And in the process, it cooks the delicate signaling proteins.

36
00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:10.330
These older extraction methods completely wipe out the biological blueprint, leaving behind

37
00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.210
useless fragments the body can no longer read.

38
00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:19.170
To safely capture these delicate proteins, founder and inventor Boris Markosian combined

39
00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:24.090
the principles of fundamental biology with the physical controls of advanced engineering.

40
00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:27.410
He built his approach by crossing traditional boundaries.

41
00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:32.490
He spent years working in fundamental cellular biology at places like the Salk Institute

42
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:36.930
and combined that with experience managing massive data systems at Google.

43
00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:41.590
By merging deep biological research with computational architecture,

44
00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:47.710
he developed a new framework capable of safely extracting the human body's operating system

45
00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:49.170
without destroying it.

46
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.730
This diagram shows the connected stack, a five-step system built to protect fragile protein

47
00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:56.390
signals.

48
00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:02.470
Step four, the ASAP AI platform, identifies exactly which protein instructions are needed.

49
00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:07.230
Step one uses cold temperature extraction to safely pull those instructions.

50
00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:12.750
Step two uses targeted lasers to shatter viruses, leaving proteins untouched.

51
00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:18.390
From mapping the data on a computer to extracting the physical material in a lab, this

52
00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.010
linked pipeline prevents the proteins from scrambling.

53
00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.770
The healing message survives intact.

54
00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.070
Once we have the preserved instructions, we need a way to mail them.

55
00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:34.690
The proteins are carefully packaged inside engineered microscopic bubbles, known as exosomes.

56
00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:40.070
Because these carriers are made of the same natural materials as human cells, they glide

57
00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.530
easily through the bloodstream,

58
00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:46.190
docking directly onto targeted tissues to deliver the repair instructions exactly where

59
00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:46.770
they belong.

60
00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.850
But getting the medicine to the right place is only half the battle.

61
00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:55.870
In a normal hospital, a patient gets a standard dose of medicine, based on a statistical

62
00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:56.550
average.

63
00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:00.950
The problem is, an average patient does not actually exist.

64
00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.830
This is where your smartwatch comes in.

65
00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:07.730
Using continuous data from everyday wearable sensors,

66
00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:13.510
the system monitors your unique biological responses in real time, building a digital

67
00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:14.410
twin of your health.

68
00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:19.670
That live data feeds straight back into the AI platform, which safely and dynamically

69
00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:25.290
adjusts your specific dose based on how your body is actually reacting, that very minute.

70
00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:30.270
The therapy constantly adapts to you, ensuring your body receives precisely the level

71
00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.930
of instruction it needs to heal, and nothing more.

72
00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:38.990
We no longer have to rely on synthetic chemicals that bully our biology into submission.

73
00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:43.830
By giving ourselves the precise, native instructions they evolve to understand,

74
00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:49.710
we empower the human body to coordinate its own repair, the future of medicine is built

75
00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.050
from the inside out.

